  "narrative": {
    "intro": "National Steel and Shipbuilding shows concentrated federal business in FY2026 to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding has $2.8B in contract obligations, spread across 16 awards with an average award size of $174M. National Steel and Shipbuilding obligations are up 406.3% year over year. National Steel and Shipbuilding received widely varying obligations in prior years: $471M in FY21, $2.2B in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.4B in FY24, and $550M in FY25. All figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Current-year totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date. This profile highlights recent scale and volatility in National Steel and Shipbuilding federal work and gives a concise baseline for procurement, capture, and program planning conversations.",
